---
prometheus:
  endpoint: "https://prometheus.example.com"
  bearer_token: ""  # Optional: leave empty if no auth required

github:
  token: ""  # Required: GitHub personal access token (ghp_...)
  default_repo: "owner/repository"  # e.g., "anthropics/anthropic-sdk-python"
  issue_labels: ["production", "incident", "p0"]  # Optional: filter issues by labels

gitlab:
  token: ""  # Required: GitLab personal access token (glpat_...)
  default_project: "group/project"  # e.g., "gitlab-org/gitlab"
  issue_labels: ["production", "incident"]  # Optional: filter issues by labels

analysis:
  commit_search_days: 30  # How far back to search git history
  max_files_to_analyze: 50  # Maximum number of files to analyze in detail
  auto_save_reports: true  # Automatically save RCA reports to files
  reports_directory: "rca-reports"  # Where to save RCA reports
---

# Thufir Configuration

This file configures the Thufir root cause analysis plugin.

## Prometheus Setup

Set your Prometheus endpoint URL. If your Prometheus instance requires authentication, provide a bearer token.

```yaml
prometheus:
  endpoint: "https://prometheus.mycompany.com"
  bearer_token: "my-secret-token"
```

**Installation:**
```bash
cd mcp-servers/prometheus
pip install -r requirements.txt
```

**Testing:**
```bash
export PROMETHEUS_URL="https://prometheus.example.com"
export PROMETHEUS_TOKEN="optional-token"
python server.py
```

## GitHub Setup

Create a personal access token with `repo` scope:
https://github.com/settings/tokens

```yaml
github:
  token: "ghp_1234567890abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz123"
  default_repo: "myorg/myrepo"
  issue_labels: ["production", "incident"]
```

GitHub uses the official MCP server: `@modelcontextprotocol/server-github`

**Installation:**
```bash
npm install -g @modelcontextprotocol/server-github
```

**Environment:**
```bash
export GITHUB_TOKEN="ghp_your_token"
```

## GitLab Setup

Create a personal access token with `api` scope:
https://gitlab.com/-/profile/personal_access_tokens

```yaml
gitlab:
  token: "glpat-1234567890ABCDEFGHIJK"
  default_project: "mygroup/myproject"
  issue_labels: ["production", "incident"]
```

**Installation:**
```bash
cd mcp-servers/gitlab
pip install -r requirements.txt
```

**Testing:**
```bash
export GITLAB_URL="https://gitlab.com"
export GITLAB_TOKEN="glpat-your-token"
export GITLAB_PROJECT_ID="12345"  # or "group/project"
python server.py
```

## Analysis Preferences

Customize how Thufir performs root cause analysis:

```yaml
analysis:
  commit_search_days: 30  # Search commits from last 30 days
  max_files_to_analyze: 50  # Limit deep analysis to 50 files
  auto_save_reports: true  # Always save RCA reports
  reports_directory: "rca-reports"  # Save reports here
```

## Usage

After configuration, Thufir commands will automatically use these settings:

```bash
# Analyze Prometheus alert (uses prometheus.endpoint from settings)
/thufir:analyze-prometheus HighErrorRate

# Analyze GitHub issue (uses github.default_repo from settings)
/thufir:analyze-github 456

# Analyze GitLab issue (uses gitlab.default_project from settings)
/thufir:analyze-gitlab 789

# Interactive investigation
/thufir:investigate
```

## Troubleshooting

**MCP servers not starting:**
- Check that dependencies are installed (`pip install -r requirements.txt`)
- Verify environment variables are set correctly
- Check Claude Code logs for MCP server errors

**Authentication errors:**
- Verify tokens have correct permissions
- Check token expiration dates
- Ensure endpoints are accessible from your network

**No data returned:**
- Verify Prometheus/GitHub/GitLab URLs are correct
- Check that default_repo/default_project exist and you have access
- Test API endpoints manually with curl

## Security Notes

- **Never commit this file to git** - it contains sensitive tokens
- Add `.claude/*.local.md` to `.gitignore`
- Use environment variables for CI/CD instead of this file
- Rotate tokens regularly
- Use read-only tokens when possible
